\begin_layout Standard
Thanks to enormous progress in the field of artificial intelligence, more
 and more problems can be taken over by machines.
 In the meantime it is not only possible to relieve humans of complex tasks
 but also to develop completely new solutions to problems.
 Learning a strategy to solve a problem without prior knowledge is adressed
 in the field of reinforcement learning (RL), where an agent has to maximise
 the expected reward in an environment.
 [xxx RL picture] The environment represents a Markov decision process,
 which is a stochastic form of determinism so that in each state, when performin
g an action, the same subsequent state is reached with a certail probability.
 The agent has only limited computing power at his disposal, which is why
 he must carefully weigh up exploration and exploitation in order to efficiently
 develop a strategy.
