\begin_layout Paragraph
closure, evaluation safety, Formeln als Gensequenz
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Closure refers to the requirement that the creation of trees always results
 in evaluable expressions.
 In order to avoid data type complications, Strongly Typed Genetic Programming
 (STGP) is mostly used nowadays, where a conversion between number and truth
 values must be done explicitly (for example, with comparison operators
 or if statements).
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "Strongly_typed_GP"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 Although this requires that all tree nodes and operators as well as terminals
 are uniquely classified into input and output types, it produces much more
 interpretable formulas that usually do not provide for automatic conversion
 of data types.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Evaluation safety poses a particular problem because even type-correct expressio
ns can be mathematically invalid.
 In the case of frequently occurring functions, the definition gaps are
 usually filled with a dummy value (division by zero, for example, with
 1).
 To avoid changing the essence of an operator too much, a tree can also
 simply be discarded in the case of rarely occurring errors.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Komplexität des Suchraumes
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Due to the high branching factor for solution candidates, the genotypic
 search space for trees must be strongly restricted.
 Thus, both the maximum tree depth and the number of nodes are usually limited.
 Formula components can also be additionally weighted to avoid complex mathemati
cal operators.
 As a multi-objective optimisation, therefore, instead of only the best
 candidate, all pareto-efficient combinations of fitness and complexity
 are stored, between which a choice can be made at the end of the run.
