\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
All IB features at a glance.
 The reward is not part of the GP-process.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "IB-observations-state"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Industrial Benchmark was introduced by scientists at Siemens to meet
 the high requirements of complex, real world industrial processes.
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "industrialBenchmark"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 It is high-dimensional 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "IB-observations-state"

\end_inset

, yet the Markov process is only partially observable, so even past values
 must also be considered.
 Since it is also very stochastic, the learning process is made even more
 difficult.
 The Reward depends on a combination of Action 0 and Action 1, as well as
 Action 2, which severely penalises misconduct.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Currently there are no good human written solutions known for the IB, but
 approaching the average value (
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

do nothing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

) is considered to be a respectably good comparison solution.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Black box: PSONN
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As black box, a particle swarm optimisation algorithm with neural networks
 (PSONN 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "PSONN_fuzzy_RL_Hein_Udluft"
literal "true"

\end_inset

) with a calculated IB reward of 
\begin_inset Formula $5353$
\end_inset

 was chosen.
 
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The initial states of the IB in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "daniel_hein_doktorarbeit"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 were randomized.
 Comparable values could be obtained by a randomized initial state, but
 the results were very volatile.
 The difference of agents in Hein's work was 7% worse on average.
 This value was used for comparison.
 For the PSONN policy, this results in a adjusted penalty value of 
\begin_inset Formula $5728/1.07=5353$
\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 Particle swarm optimisation algorithms, similar to GP, can find solutions
 for many types of problems.
 The solution space is populated by a swarm population, which should find
 the best optima by swarm intelligence.
 This approach is very interesting as a black box, because even bulky solution
 models can be found relatively quickly.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Mountain Car
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Black box Sarsa-200 vs Sarsa-75
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As a black box solution, the leader of the gym-leaderboards was chosen,
 which uses a SARSA approach with tiling and required 75 training episodes
 to find a sufficient policy with an average reward of 
\begin_inset Formula $-103.41$
\end_inset

.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "xiao2019"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 At this state, the agent is still a very inexperienced with generally poor
 exploration, coupled with complete areas of bad decisions like reversing
 shortly before the goal in some cases as can be seen in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sarsa75_problem_decision_plots"

\end_inset

.
 Especially for sensitive areas, more emphasis would be placed on security.
 These cases are rare and do not influence the average result significantly,
 which can be seen in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "img:MTC-heuristic-vs-sarsa-reward"

\end_inset

, but represent a risk.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The same approach was therefore trained and analysed after 200 steps, where
 uncertainties play a much smaller role and the performance increases accordingl
y by almost 5 steps to 
\begin_inset Formula $\approx-98.7$
\end_inset

.
 Further training did not lead to further improvements; on the contrary,
 they deteriorated strongly, which is also reflected in irregularities in
 the plots, see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "sarsa1000-plots"

\end_inset

, what might be caused to the non-convergence of Sarsa approaches.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The gym-environment has a leaderboard containing the approaches that have
 been able to learn the fastest to create a policy that solves the problem
 in steps of less than 
\begin_inset Formula $110$
\end_inset

.
 As the leaderboard only evaluates how quickly the goal is achieved, but
 not how secure the approaches are.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "https://github.com/openai/gym/wiki/Leaderboard"
target "https://github.com/openai/gym/wiki/Leaderboard"
literal "false"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset

 
\end_layout

